# Reproduction only for inc-8mg9; no game-code or data changes.
# Read by tools/check_find_traps_cap.sh (bead inc-b4l3g.17). Run from the repo root:
# INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/orc-priest-seed1-opt0822.char \
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_RUN_DIR="$PWD/logs/inc-8mg9/control-fresh" \
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/find-traps-control.keys 1
# Route: the priest is LOADED from the frozen fixture orc-priest-seed1-opt0822
# (Priest 1, god Aiswin, domains Fate/Knowledge/Night), never generated: chargen
# offers a different screen on some seeds. A loaded game opens no prompt, so the
# first key is 'w'. No G is pressed: the priest stays level 1.
# Learn Any Spell sets SP_INNATE. CalcEffect (src/Magic.cpp:633-641) therefore
# uses ChallengeRating (sum of class levels), then adds BONUS_SCHOOL_CASTING_LEVEL
# for Divination: the Fate domain grants +1 (lib/domains.irh:296), so
# effective Find Traps caster level is 2 (1 + 1), below the cap.
# Observed Search: +0 before, +2 after, delta +2.
# Wizard Mode Switches rows have no menu letters, so @cursorto cannot find them:
# DOWN counts from the top row (Cheat Death), and the check greps the switches
# dump for YES on all four rows. Free Advancement is row 3, Ignore Spell Failure
# row 6, Infinite Mana row 8, Freeze Monsters row 11.
# W writes full sheets beneath the run's logs/; @dump captures skill totals.
# Search has zero ranks and is omitted from the full sheet before the cast.
# ESC y aborts the skill manager without allocating any ranks.
w y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*2 SPACE # Free Advancement
DOWN*3 SPACE # Ignore Spell Failure
DOWN*2 SPACE # Infinite Mana
DOWN*3 SPACE # Freeze Monsters
@dump:switches
ESC
w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Find Traps" ENTER
d
@dump:sheet-before
W
"find-traps-before" ENTER
S
@cursorto:mark "Searching" DOWN
@dump:search-before
ESC y
ESC
m
@choose "Find Traps"
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:cast
d
@dump:sheet-after
W
"find-traps-after" ENTER
S
@cursorto:mark "Searching" DOWN
@dump:search-after
ESC y
ESC
@quit
